# NFR Requirements — Unit: pr-review-agent

## Security (SECURITY extension — ENABLED, blocking)

Mapping of applicable Security Baseline rules to this unit. Rules not relevant to a CI review agent are marked N/A.

| Rule | Applicability | Requirement for this unit |
|---|---|---|
| SECURITY-03 (App logging) | Applicable | Structured logs with level/message; **never** log `KIRO_API_KEY`, `GH_TOKEN`, or full diff at INFO. Diff only at DEBUG. |
| SECURITY-05 (Input validation) | Applicable | PR diff + Kiro CLI output are untrusted. Validate/parse CLI JSON defensively; use `subprocess` arg lists (no shell string interpolation) to prevent command injection. |
| SECURITY-06 (Least privilege) | Applicable | `GITHUB_TOKEN` scoped to: PR read, issue/PR comment write, checks/statuses write, PR review write. `KIRO_API_KEY` exposed only to the review job. No AWS IAM added. |
| SECURITY-10 (Supply chain) | Applicable | Pin `kiro-cli` version, pin all GitHub Actions to SHA/tag, pin Python deps to exact versions. No `latest`. |
| SECURITY-13 (Integrity) | Applicable | Kiro CLI binary downloaded from official source; workflow file access-controlled like other workflows; CLI output parsed with safe JSON (no eval/deserialization of untrusted objects). |
| SECURITY-15 (Exception handling / fail-safe) | Applicable | All external calls (gh CLI, kiro CLI subprocess) wrapped in error handling; **fail closed** (status check FAILS) on any error; global handler sets ERROR verdict; timeout enforced (300s). |
| SECURITY-01 (Encryption at rest/in transit) | N/A | No data store; the agent persists nothing. GitHub/Kiro traffic is HTTPS by the tools. |
| SECURITY-02 (Network intermediary logging) | N/A | No load balancer / API gateway / CDN introduced. |
| SECURITY-04 (HTTP security headers) | N/A | No HTML-serving endpoint. |
| SECURITY-07 (Network config) | N/A | Runs on existing CodeBuild runner; no new network resources. |
| SECURITY-08 (App access control) | N/A | No application endpoints exposed. |
| SECURITY-09 (Hardening) | Partial/Applicable | No default creds; error output to PR is generic (no stack traces leaked into comments). |
| SECURITY-11 (Secure design) | Applicable | Prompt-injection defense (BR-PRA-12) + constrained CLI tool posture; review logic isolated in dedicated module. |
| SECURITY-12 (AuthN/credential mgmt) | Applicable | No hardcoded credentials; `KIRO_API_KEY` + `GH_TOKEN` via secrets only. |
| SECURITY-14 (Alerting/monitoring) | Partial | Workflow run status is visible in GitHub Actions UI; failures surface as failed checks. Formal alerting is out of scope for a CI review agent (documented). |

## Performance & Cost
- **PERF-01**: Oversized-PR guard skips review when diff > `MAX_DIFF_BYTES` (default ~200 KB, Q3=B), bounding CLI cost/latency.
- **PERF-02**: A single review invocation is bounded by `REVIEW_TIMEOUT_SECONDS` (default 300s / 5 min, Q4=A); exceeding it is a fail-closed error.
- **PERF-03**: Target end-to-end review time for typical PRs: a few minutes.

## Reliability / Error Handling
- **REL-01**: Fail-closed on any unrecoverable error (BR-PRA-08); the status check never passes silently on failure.
- **REL-02**: Idempotent comment posting (BR-PRA-14) — re-runs update the agent's existing comment, no duplicates.
- **REL-03**: Kiro CLI exit codes checked (0 ok; 1 failure; 2 arg error) → non-zero maps to ERROR verdict.

## Observability
- **OBS-01**: Log a structured decision summary: findings count by severity + final verdict (no secrets, SECURITY-03).
- **OBS-02**: The GitHub status check description communicates the verdict succinctly (e.g., "3 findings (1 High) — changes requested").

## Maintainability / Testability
- **MNT-01**: Pure logic (`compute_verdict`, `classify_findings`, `parse_cli_response`, `render_summary`) isolated from I/O for unit + property testing.
- **MNT-02**: PBT (Hypothesis) for identified properties (PBT-01 set) + example-based pytest for critical scenarios (PBT-10).
- **MNT-03**: Configuration via env vars (table in tech-stack-decisions.md) — no hardcoded thresholds.

